{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/974048-the-pack-the-lodge-of-crows","id":974048,"title":"[The Pack] The Lodge of Crows","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-21T15:01:43-07:00","id":974048,"title":"[The Pack] The Lodge of Crows","content":"On pg 77 of &quot;The Pack&quot;, each of the tribes 3 Pillar lodges are listed, along with the sacred prey they hunt. However, the Lodge of Crows - one of my very favorite Lodges from 1e - is the only one that doesn't specific what their sacred Prey actually is. It's also one of those Lodges whose original write-up doesn't easily translate to the new Sacred Prey focus of the Storm Lords, as it's whole purpose was to enforce the leadership of the Storm Lords from the shadows.<br /> <br /> Any ideas on how they might translate in 2e?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:06:42-07:00","id":974052,"title":"","content":"It seems to just be a variation of how they hunt, rather than what they hunt, similar to the Thousand Steel Teeth and the Wendigo. Presumably they share the sacred prey of all Storm Lords, the Claimed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:11:26-07:00","id":974055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/974048-the-pack-the-lodge-of-crows?p=974052#post974052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It seems to just be a variation of how they hunt, rather than what they hunt, similar to the Thousand Steel Teeth and the Wendigo. Presumably they share the sacred prey of all Storm Lords, the Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, I figured that might be the case but there is the example of the Lodge of Wrath who simply focus on anyone who violates their territory, so I wasn't sure. Anything that would require them to be focused on the Claimed would require a ground-up re-imaging of what the Lodge of Crows is all about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:24:12-07:00","id":974063,"title":"","content":"Something that the Lodge of Crows likely has if we do a parallel with the lodge from 1e is the capacity to attain the Connected Condition with minimum effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T15:46:48-07:00","id":974075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/974048-the-pack-the-lodge-of-crows?p=974055#post974055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I figured that might be the case but there is the example of the Lodge of Wrath who simply focus on anyone who violates their territory, so I wasn't sure. Anything that would require them to be focused on the Claimed would require a ground-up re-imaging of what the Lodge of Crows is all about.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sacred prey doesn't mean only prey. If the focus is on the sacred prey in a lodge, it's likely to be more important to hunt them, but at a tribal level it isn't a 'them or nothing' deal, and Storm Lords can hunt anything they want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-21T23:21:20-07:00","id":974258,"title":"","content":"Maybe it's a bit heresy to say, but could not Lodge of Crow hunt 'weakness'? It would nicely work with as is Storm Lords philosophy and have logical implications of Crows to mingle in all Tribes affairs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T05:58:17-07:00","id":974357,"title":"","content":"This is crazy, I was just talking with my friends about the Lodge of Crows last week! Basically, my idea is that the Lodge acts like an Investment Banking Firm to mortals(I get tired of biotech being rehashed over and over again in the gamelines), but they use their connections and influence to hunt Claimed/Urged/Possessed at the upper echelons of power. Not every Claimed is a homeless bum running around whacking random people. Greed, Commerce, and Business spirits exist and people looking to amass huge fortunes are ripe for the picking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-22T08:20:45-07:00","id":974424,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar717_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"717\" data-vbnamecard=\"717\">Monghani</a>, both of those ideas are interesting. I was personally thinking along the lines of the following options for their sacred prey:<ul><li>oathbreakers</li> <li>only those enemies who have been confronted by the forsaken before and emerged victorious. (in keeping with the idea that they pursue vengeance as if it were a sacred virtue)</li> <li>their sacred prey is groups or institutions, never individuals. They can call the sacred hunt on a band of hunters or a the primogen council, but never just a lone hunter or a single vampire.</li> <li>lastly, perhaps the exact opposite of the above; only those who accumulate power for strictly personal gain. Like the Lodge of Garm they target the powerful, but they use different means, attacking and testing enemies and &quot;friends&quot; alike through secrecy, temptation, influence, and cunning and will usually call off their hunt if the target proves himself to be virtuous and worthy.</li> </ul>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-03T09:22:23-07:00","id":980812,"title":"","content":"My intent for the Lodge of Crows is that they're one of the Lodges that refine their hunt via <i>method </i>rather than <i>prey</i>. Yes, as a Storm Lord-dominated Lodge, they often focus on Claimed, but not exclusively to such. The Crows do things cleverly, via connections and influence; they see the sacred hunt through that lens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T08:34:58-07:00","id":982141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/974048-the-pack-the-lodge-of-crows?p=980812#post980812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My intent for the Lodge of Crows is that they're one of the Lodges that refine their hunt via <i>method </i>rather than <i>prey</i>. Yes, as a Storm Lord-dominated Lodge, they often focus on Claimed, but not exclusively to such. The Crows do things cleverly, via connections and influence; they see the sacred hunt through that lens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, something along those lines would certainly be the easiest way to make a lodge more in line with 2e in general, but it's such a drastic change to the nature and purpose of the Lodge of Crows as described in 1e that I feel like i'd be inclined to dislike it. Of course, seeing an actual official write-up could totally change my opinion - i'd certainly rather pay for an official writeup to react to and riff of off than nothing at all. At this point it's just difficult to visualize how the focus away from their original role to hunting Claimed (which is about as far from their original concern as can be imagined) wouldn't fundamentally change almost everything about them to the extent that they don't resemble the original lodge much at all.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T11:15:13-07:00","id":982218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EmanantVolition</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/974048-the-pack-the-lodge-of-crows?p=982141#post982141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, something along those lines would certainly be the easiest way to make a lodge more in line with 2e in general, but it's such a drastic change to the nature and purpose of the Lodge of Crows as described in 1e that I feel like i'd be inclined to dislike it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. Have we read the same Lodge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-05T15:21:57-07:00","id":982390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/974048-the-pack-the-lodge-of-crows?p=982218#post982218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, it's not. Have we read the same Lodge?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't know, have we?<br /> <br /> The original &quot;Three Pillars&quot; were focused on Urdaga politics in general, and Iminir hegemony in particular. At least, that is always the reading I came away with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/358-emanantvolition","name":"EmanantVolition","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}